<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moravian-Silesian Land</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1928">1928</a>–<a href="/years/1949">1949</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Moravian-Silesian Land was one of the four lands of interwar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a>, created in 1928 by merging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-silesia">Czech Silesia</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brno">Brno</a>. Part of its territory was annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in 1938. Restored after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, it was abolished by the communist regime with effect from 1949, when the historic lands were replaced by regions.</p></div>
